## Backup and Disaster Recovery

{{- if ne .DatabaseDriver ""}}
### Database Backup

**1. Automated Backup:**
```bash
#!/bin/bash
# backup-database.sh
DATE=$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)
BACKUP_FILE="{{.ProjectName | lower}}_backup_$DATE.sql"

{{- if eq .DatabaseDriver "postgres"}}
pg_dump $DATABASE_URL > $BACKUP_FILE
{{- else if eq .DatabaseDriver "mysql"}}
mysqldump --single-transaction --routines --triggers $DATABASE_NAME > $BACKUP_FILE
{{- end}}

# Upload to cloud storage
aws s3 cp $BACKUP_FILE s3://backups/{{.ProjectName | lower}}/
```

**2. Kubernetes CronJob:**
```yaml
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata:
  name: {{.ProjectName | lower}}-backup
  namespace: {{.ProjectName | lower}}
spec:
  schedule: "0 2 * * *"
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:
          containers:
          - name: backup
            image: postgres:13
            command:
            - /bin/bash
            - -c
            - pg_dump $DATABASE_URL | gzip > /backup/{{.ProjectName | lower}}_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S).sql.gz
            env:
            - name: DATABASE_URL
              valueFrom:
                secretKeyRef:
                  name: {{.ProjectName | lower}}-secrets
                  key: database-url
            volumeMounts:
            - name: backup-storage
              mountPath: /backup
          restartPolicy: OnFailure
          volumes:
          - name: backup-storage
            persistentVolumeClaim:
              claimName: backup-pvc
```
{{- end}}

